//! Fitted SILK-to-48 kHz resampling filters.
//!
//! RFC 6716 §4.2.9 makes the resampler non-normative. For the three SILK
//! rates to 48 kHz these polyphase filters were identified by least squares
//! from the official test vectors used as black-box data (testvector02,
//! 03 and 04: this crate's SILK output at the internal rate against the
//! reference decoder's 48 kHz output; see `tests/fit_resampler.rs`), so
//! that this decoder's SILK and hybrid output follows the reference's
//! resampler in delay and response. Output sample `L*m + p` is
//! `sum_k FIT[p][k] * x[m - k]`.

#![allow(clippy::excessive_precision, clippy::unreadable_literal)]

